1
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:38,920
ADAPTED FROM <i>THE EARLY SPRING</i> ON JJWXC.NET
AUTHOR: GU NIANG BIE KU

3
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:45,160
- Morning.
- Morning, Mr. Luan.

4
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:47,320
Can I clean your office now?

5
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:48,720
Yes.

6
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:53,800
Shang Zhitao.

7
00:01:55,160 --> 00:01:57,040
Why didn't you send me
the meeting minutes of the business trip?

8
00:01:58,160 --> 00:01:59,360
If you have forgotten about it,

9
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:01,200
then you can consider resigning today.

10
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:02,520
I did send it to you.

11
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:04,560
I finished everything that night,

12
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:05,840
and I sent it to you and Lumi.

13
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:07,760
Where did you send it?
I didn't receive anything.

14
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:08,960
Your e-mail.

15
00:02:09,639 --> 00:02:11,320
I did send it.

16
00:02:14,520 --> 00:02:15,760
There's another Luke in the company.

17
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:17,760
Are you aware of that?

18
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:20,560
Luke Liu.

19
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:22,160
Check your mailbox.

20
00:02:22,760 --> 00:02:24,720
If you sent it to the wrong recipient,
that would be a breach of confidentiality.

21
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:25,880
That's worse than forgetting to send it.

22
00:02:30,160 --> 00:02:31,160
Now, make sure

23
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:33,120
to send your resignation letter
to the right address.

24
00:02:38,440 --> 00:02:40,840
Luke Liu?

25
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:48,520
REPAYING FAVOR WITH YOUR LIFE

26
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:56,800
- Flora.
- Lumi.

27
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:58,360
The filming proposal has been approved.

28
00:02:58,440 --> 00:03:00,240
We'll head to the location tomorrow.

29
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:01,280
But I checked the weather forecast,

30
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:03,160
and it says there will be
a heavy rainstorm tomorrow.

31
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:05,160
You know what? In a while,

32
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:07,080
we'll discuss the filming
contingency plan with Luke.

33
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:08,080
I…

34
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:09,720
Can I still join?

35
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:11,360
Of course.

36
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:13,000
I've talked to Luke.

37
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:14,520
You'll come with me.

38
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:19,000
But I sent the e-mail to the wrong person.

39
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:21,200
God knows if I can stay here or not.

40
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:23,080
Listen.

41
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:26,360
Just do two things well.

42
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:29,040
Firstly, do what you need to do.

43
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:30,440
Ace the filming of this commercial.

44
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:31,880
Secondly,

45
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:34,760
forget what Luke said.

46
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:38,280
So I won't be fired?

47
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:40,200
You won't.

48
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:42,400
If they fire you,
who is going to work for me?

49
00:03:42,480 --> 00:03:44,800
Besides, we're having
the filming tomorrow.

50
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:47,120
It's too late to onboard a new person.

51
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:48,800
Don't worry.

52
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:51,160
I'll help you stay.

53
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:53,960
- Thank you, Lumi.
- Sure.

54
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:05,320
You work at Lime now?

55
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:08,120
But

56
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:10,440
I don't know if I'll pass the probation.

57
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:11,680
Thank you.

58
00:04:12,640 --> 00:04:13,640
Getting into Lime

59
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:15,400
already gives you bragging rights
at your alma mater.

60
00:04:16,399 --> 00:04:18,040
To survive in Beijing,

61
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:19,320
you have to go through trial and error.

62
00:04:19,839 --> 00:04:21,680
If you fail, you pay for the lesson.

63
00:04:21,760 --> 00:04:25,080
If you succeed, celebrate it. Drink it.

64
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:30,120
Oh. How's your boyfriend, Xin Zhaozhou?

65
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:31,280
Where is he working?

66
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,080
We broke up before graduation.

67
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:40,360
His mom wanted him
to apply to be a civil servant.

68
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:43,960
He asked me to move with him,
but I said no.

69
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:45,560
He could travel.

70
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:47,320
Why couldn't he move to Beijing?

71
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:50,880
That's just life, I guess.

72
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:53,040
He wants to stay in the south.
I want to stay in the north.

73
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:55,080
We don't have a choice.

74
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:57,680
It's okay.

75
00:04:57,760 --> 00:05:00,920
Lime has the classiest men
in all of Beijing.

76
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:03,240
Have a few relationships.

77
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:05,280
Experience them while you're young.

78
00:05:11,760 --> 00:05:12,760
It's my boss.

79
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:14,000
I have to take this.

80
00:05:17,760 --> 00:05:18,920
Hi. This is the dessert to go.

81
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,680
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

82
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:24,000
I knew it. My client suddenly arrived.
I need to head back now.

83
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:26,720
I packed two portions. Take them with you.

84
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:27,880
You barely ate.

85
00:05:28,760 --> 00:05:31,120
Keep one for yourself.

86
00:05:32,280 --> 00:05:33,720
I only found out
that you had already footed the bill

87
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:35,120
when I asked them to pack the food.

88
00:05:35,200 --> 00:05:37,240
But I told you it would be my treat.

89
00:05:37,320 --> 00:05:39,200
Buying me a meal
when you just found a job?

90
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:40,320
Come on.

91
00:05:41,640 --> 00:05:42,800
Thanks.

92
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:47,560
You have already outperformed

93
00:05:47,640 --> 00:05:51,000
95% of fresh graduates
by coming to Beijing alone.

94
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:53,600
Tao, you can do this. Make sure you stay.

95
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:56,640
When you're inside,
you always stand a chance.

96
00:05:57,240 --> 00:05:58,440
Don't worry.

97
00:05:58,520 --> 00:06:00,160
I will see it through.

98
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:16,000
Lumi.

99
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:18,280
Are you okay? Are you unwell?

100
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:21,560
They can't confirm
the filming site with me.

101
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:23,520
It's annoying.

102
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:26,080
Plus, I'm on my period. My tummy hurts.

103
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:27,240
Come.

104
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:30,120
Drink this. I brought goji berry brew.

105
00:06:30,200 --> 00:06:32,000
Have some. While it's hot.

106
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:34,040
When push comes to shove,
we'll stop somewhere.

107
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:36,000
Take a break. Don't act tough.

108
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:38,000
It's fine. I can endure this.

109
00:06:38,080 --> 00:06:39,800
We need to set everything up early.

110
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:41,600
Luke might drop by at night.

111
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:42,600
He…

112
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:45,160
He's coming?

113
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:51,160
Don't be so anxious.

114
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:53,120
He just has high standards.

115
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:54,920
He sounds mean, but he isn't.

116
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,080
You'll see why working with him

117
00:06:56,160 --> 00:06:58,360
is a good thing as time goes by.

118
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:02,480
Luke is not the hypocritical sort.

119
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:10,160
Thank you.

120
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:19,120
TAOBAO

121
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:20,120
Look.

122
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:31,840
Don't tell me

123
00:07:31,920 --> 00:07:34,320
- you brought your own bedding.
- I did.

124
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:37,560
I expected a basic living condition,
given that it's a village,

125
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:39,560
but I didn't expect it to be this bad.

126
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:41,720
You're provident.

127
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:43,280
I'm impressed.

128
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:45,080
You have a bright future ahead of you.

129
00:07:45,160 --> 00:07:47,480
- Can I have this?
- Take it.

130
00:07:57,880 --> 00:07:58,720
Lumi,

131
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:00,440
I'll check the next village

132
00:08:00,520 --> 00:08:02,440
to see if they have hot water.
I'll bring some to you.

133
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:04,000
Don't make your bed. Just lie down.

134
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:05,120
I'll help you later.

135
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:28,960
Mr. Liu.

136
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:31,240
Cancel today's itinerary. Just go back.

137
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:36,799
Lumi.

138
00:08:36,880 --> 00:08:39,320
I got you two bottles of hot water.

139
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,000
I was thinking

140
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:42,679
I'll prepare cup noodles for you.

141
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:44,039
Okay? You can eat something.

142
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:45,480
Are you serious?

143
00:08:47,520 --> 00:08:50,920
I think you just saved my life.

144
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:06,520
The bag!

145
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:10,080
<i>Mister. Quick.</i>

146
00:09:10,160 --> 00:09:11,880
<i>To the filming site. Now.</i>

147
00:09:16,480 --> 00:09:18,440
‪-Coming through.
‪-Over here.

148
00:09:18,520 --> 00:09:20,400
We need to confirm the time with him.

149
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:21,880
It's mainly because of the weather.

150
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:23,560
I checked the weather forecast.

151
00:09:23,640 --> 00:09:25,680
It says it won't rain,
but it's cloudy now.

152
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:45,520
We'll start shooting
when the actors are here.

153
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:46,960
- Okay.
- Lumi.

154
00:09:47,040 --> 00:09:48,920
Tracy sent me over to help out.

155
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
I'm Kitty, from Division Three.

156
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:56,000
Kitty, is it?

157
00:09:56,080 --> 00:09:57,600
The Excel sheet
is in the shared OA system.

158
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:58,520
- Okay.
- Take a look.

159
00:09:58,600 --> 00:10:00,200
We'll have a meeting
with the director later

160
00:10:00,280 --> 00:10:02,240
- to confirm the plan before we shoot.
- Okay.

161
00:10:02,320 --> 00:10:03,600
This is Shang Zhitao from my division.

162
00:10:04,880 --> 00:10:05,960
Hello.

163
00:10:08,680 --> 00:10:09,640
Still unwell?

164
00:10:10,160 --> 00:10:11,160
Let's go to the hospital.

165
00:10:11,240 --> 00:10:12,720
It's fine. I just need to sit for a while.

166
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:14,640
Show this to her. Bring her up to date.

167
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:17,440
Kitty., hold the fort here.

168
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:19,040
I'll take Lumi back first.

169
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:20,200
And take a look at this.

170
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:21,120
- Okay.
- Thank you.

171
00:10:21,920 --> 00:10:23,840
Come. I'm done.

172
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:25,120
Let's go to the hospital.
Stop acting tough.

173
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:26,160
- I'm fine.
- Come.

174
00:10:26,240 --> 00:10:27,320
I…

175
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:28,320
Call me if anything comes up.

176
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:29,320
Okay.

177
00:10:33,760 --> 00:10:35,760
Did someone corner you at home again?

178
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:41,160
It must be Zhang Xin.

179
00:10:41,240 --> 00:10:42,400
She came to my shop once.

180
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:45,000
I said you and I were no longer friends
and asked her to leave.

181
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:47,480
How does she know where I live?

182
00:10:48,160 --> 00:10:50,080
I'm not surprised.

183
00:10:50,160 --> 00:10:52,440
Women become Sherlock Holmes
when they are obsessed with you.

184
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:53,720
It's easy to find where you live.

185
00:10:54,400 --> 00:10:56,200
You should head to your parents' mansion

186
00:10:56,280 --> 00:10:58,400
in the suburb and hide there.

187
00:10:58,480 --> 00:10:59,520
We'll see.

188
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:02,400
I have to head to the filming site
and take a walk there.

189
00:11:02,920 --> 00:11:05,200
- I'll take your car.
- Go ahead. Drive safe.

190
00:11:06,640 --> 00:11:09,200
No wonder you're rich.

191
00:11:09,280 --> 00:11:10,720
You can earn money
while running away from a girl.

192
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:12,880
Drive safe.

193
00:11:14,120 --> 00:11:16,480
Guys, we have to make it quick today.
Finish it while the sun is up.

194
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:17,640
It'll rain soon.

195
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:18,640
Yes, Mr. Director.

196
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:19,800
Attention!

197
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:21,160
Wrap it up while the sun is up!

198
00:11:21,240 --> 00:11:22,400
Kitty.

199
00:11:22,480 --> 00:11:24,800
I thought we were supposed
to have the meeting when I came back.

200
00:11:24,880 --> 00:11:26,080
Time is running out.

201
00:11:26,160 --> 00:11:27,440
The director said
it'd rain in the afternoon,

202
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:29,160
so I had them start earlier.

203
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:33,200
You must be new.

204
00:11:33,280 --> 00:11:34,400
First time leading a project?

205
00:11:35,280 --> 00:11:36,800
- Yes.
- Oh.

206
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:38,600
The director said

207
00:11:38,680 --> 00:11:40,040
there are some backup props
we haven't bought.

208
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:43,200
The driver told me
you had been here before.

209
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:44,800
I need to make some important calls.

210
00:11:44,880 --> 00:11:47,960
Can I bother you to buy those props?

211
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:51,640
Sure.

212
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:53,440
Hold the fort then.

213
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:55,840
- Keep me updated in the group chat.
- I don't need you to tell me that.

214
00:12:00,160 --> 00:12:05,400
COSTUME DEPARTMENT

215
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:11,720
<i>Strong precipitation is expected</i>
<i>in the next few hours.</i>

216
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:13,880
<i>Please take the necessary precautions.</i>

217
00:12:17,560 --> 00:12:18,760
Kitty.

218
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:20,200
- I bought the props.
- Good.

219
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:22,080
The actor for the evening scene

220
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:24,600
complained that our accommodation
was too bad. They refused to come here.

221
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:27,600
Can you check if there are
better accommodations nearby?

222
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:30,840
The accommodation is very bad.
I understand why they complain.

223
00:12:30,920 --> 00:12:32,120
Sure.

224
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:39,000
Mister, how long till we get there?

225
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:40,760
That village is quite remote.

226
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:42,120
But worry not,

227
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:43,520
it's exactly what you're looking for.

228
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:45,760
If the room is decent,

229
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:48,520
ask more villagers to spare us some rooms.

230
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:49,880
With a beautiful lady
like you staying over,

231
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:53,800
everyone will prepare their beds nicely
and warm them up for you.

232
00:13:07,160 --> 00:13:08,200
‪Hello, Mr. Luan.

233
00:13:08,280 --> 00:13:09,240
Hello, Mr. Luan.

234
00:13:11,880 --> 00:13:12,720
Hello, Mr. Luan.

235
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:14,960
- Hello, Mr. Luan.
- Hello, Mr. Luan.

236
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:17,760
Mr. Luan, what brought you here?

237
00:13:17,840 --> 00:13:19,360
Where are Lumi and Shang Zhitao?

238
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:22,320
Lumi is sick.

239
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:25,000
Flora went to find new accommodation.
She hasn't returned yet.

240
00:13:27,880 --> 00:13:30,440
The accommodation we found was quite bad.

241
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:32,040
The actors don't want to stay there,

242
00:13:32,120 --> 00:13:33,560
and their car has broken down.

243
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:35,000
The other cars
are at the foot of the mountain,

244
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:38,760
so I asked a villager
to find new accommodation with Flora.

245
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:40,280
Why didn't you go?

246
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:42,760
We agreed on the work delegation.

247
00:13:42,840 --> 00:13:44,640
What makes you think
you can delegate work?

248
00:14:09,040 --> 00:14:12,800
<i>Sorry. The user you called</i>
<i>cannot be reached.</i>

249
00:14:12,880 --> 00:14:14,320
<i>Please try again later.</i>

250
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:19,240
<i>Stop the shoot. Be on standby.</i>

251
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:20,400
- <i>Call the police. Find her.</i>
- Shang Zhitao!

252
00:14:20,480 --> 00:14:21,440
Shang Zhitao!

253
00:14:22,520 --> 00:14:23,920
<i>The girl looking for rooms</i>
<i>went to the mountain.</i>

254
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,320
<i>The back mountain is full of steep slopes.</i>
<i>It might collapse anytime.</i>

255
00:14:26,400 --> 00:14:27,800
<i>There could also be rockfalls.</i>

256
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:29,160
<i>You'll die if you go in.</i>

257
00:14:31,520 --> 00:14:32,840
It's just right in front.

258
00:14:32,920 --> 00:14:35,280
Once we're in the village,
we'll find a shelter first.

259
00:14:35,360 --> 00:14:37,000
Once the rain stops,
I'll ride back with you.

260
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:46,120
Mister. The rain is too heavy.

261
00:14:46,200 --> 00:14:48,000
Let's turn back. Just forget it.

262
00:14:48,080 --> 00:14:49,600
I have not seen this road before.

263
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:51,520
This isn't how we came here.

264
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:54,120
It's raining. This is a shortcut.

265
00:14:55,640 --> 00:14:57,040
The road condition is awful.

266
00:14:57,120 --> 00:14:58,480
Just cling to me.

267
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,520
- Come. Come.
- Hey, you…

268
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:02,280
Come.

269
00:16:41,040 --> 00:16:42,640
LANDSLIDE WARNING, NO ENTRY

270
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:40,760
Luan Nian!

271
00:18:42,720 --> 00:18:43,720
Luan Nian!

272
00:18:49,360 --> 00:18:50,200
Luan Nian!

273
00:18:51,840 --> 00:18:53,800
Luan Nian! Luan Nian!

274
00:18:58,560 --> 00:18:59,440
It's dangerous here.

275
00:18:59,520 --> 00:19:00,680
Find a safe place first.

276
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:09,600
Forget about me. Go now.

277
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:14,960
Go now!

278
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:32,280
Shang Zhitao.

279
00:19:57,800 --> 00:19:58,640
Are you okay?

280
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:01,240
I just sprained my ankle.

281
00:20:01,320 --> 00:20:02,880
It hurts when I move.

282
00:20:08,080 --> 00:20:09,040
Your hand is bleeding.

283
00:20:13,800 --> 00:20:14,880
Hang in there.

284
00:20:15,640 --> 00:20:17,120
We should get out as soon as possible.

285
00:20:17,200 --> 00:20:18,320
There might be landslides.

286
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:26,480
Put these on.

287
00:20:49,040 --> 00:20:50,120
Did I do it right?

288
00:20:51,080 --> 00:20:52,520
There are falling rocks.

289
00:20:55,240 --> 00:20:56,560
We have to take another route.

290
00:21:13,320 --> 00:21:15,560
Listen to my command later.
Do not thrash around.

291
00:21:16,800 --> 00:21:19,080
No matter what happens, do not let go.

292
00:21:41,200 --> 00:21:42,200
Hug me tightly.

293
00:22:06,880 --> 00:22:07,800
Slowly.

294
00:22:09,280 --> 00:22:10,520
Let's rest here.

295
00:22:12,880 --> 00:22:13,840
Are we safe now?

296
00:22:14,960 --> 00:22:15,920
For now, yes.

297
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:19,160
There should be a village right in front.

298
00:22:25,560 --> 00:22:26,600
Sit down.

299
00:22:32,840 --> 00:22:33,840
How come you came?

300
00:22:37,360 --> 00:22:39,320
Venturing alone in this remote place?

301
00:22:40,240 --> 00:22:42,360
Must a rookie like you work
this hard even in this dire situation?

302
00:22:43,960 --> 00:22:45,760
No one could reach you,
so everyone came to find you.

303
00:22:47,400 --> 00:22:49,040
Fortunately, you are fine.

304
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:50,840
Put this on.

305
00:23:00,040 --> 00:23:02,640
Sorry. I've troubled
the company once again.

306
00:23:14,480 --> 00:23:16,680
It might hurt a little. Bear with me.

307
00:23:43,040 --> 00:23:43,920
Thank you.

308
00:24:01,560 --> 00:24:03,720
Don't move. I'm more cautious
than you are.

309
00:24:03,800 --> 00:24:05,240
If you become a cripple,

310
00:24:05,760 --> 00:24:07,440
you can always come to work
in your wheelchair.

311
00:24:25,520 --> 00:24:26,920
You're injured.

312
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:28,560
It's quite serious.

313
00:24:28,640 --> 00:24:29,480
I'm fine.

314
00:24:35,480 --> 00:24:37,560
We're in the same boat.

315
00:24:38,240 --> 00:24:39,240
Let me dress the wound for you.

316
00:24:55,960 --> 00:24:56,800
Sorry.

317
00:24:58,160 --> 00:24:59,000
I'm fine.

318
00:25:10,960 --> 00:25:11,800
Does it hurt?

319
00:25:59,960 --> 00:26:01,040
Get up.

320
00:26:10,640 --> 00:26:11,480
Take this.

321
00:26:17,080 --> 00:26:18,280
Come.

322
00:26:38,040 --> 00:26:41,560
When I was stuck inside,

323
00:26:41,640 --> 00:26:42,720
I felt hopeless.

324
00:26:43,280 --> 00:26:44,640
I thought

325
00:26:46,240 --> 00:26:50,000
that for my first project in Lime,
I would be on the social news.

326
00:26:52,080 --> 00:26:53,080
In my projects,

327
00:26:53,920 --> 00:26:55,760
only my client's ads
get to be on the news.

328
00:26:56,640 --> 00:26:57,560
Not my subordinates.

329
00:26:59,760 --> 00:27:01,040
I was also thinking

330
00:27:02,800 --> 00:27:06,960
that I would die, but I hadn't left
any last words for my parents.

331
00:27:09,480 --> 00:27:10,520
What would you have said?

332
00:27:11,920 --> 00:27:13,600
I…

333
00:27:13,680 --> 00:27:15,920
I would never have the chance
to repay their kindness.

334
00:27:16,000 --> 00:27:17,440
And back then, I was craving

335
00:27:17,520 --> 00:27:19,680
my dad's braised fish.

336
00:27:22,600 --> 00:27:24,600
You barely escaped,

337
00:27:24,680 --> 00:27:26,200
and you now want to kill a fish?

338
00:27:26,280 --> 00:27:27,760
But didn't they say

339
00:27:28,440 --> 00:27:30,200
eating fish makes you smarter?

340
00:27:30,280 --> 00:27:32,840
I want to be smart and stay at Lime

341
00:27:32,920 --> 00:27:34,080
to learn from you.

342
00:27:38,520 --> 00:27:39,840
How did you know

343
00:27:40,360 --> 00:27:41,800
to hit the corner
of the window to smash it open?

344
00:27:42,520 --> 00:27:45,640
I saw it on the news.
I didn't know it'd work.

345
00:27:48,080 --> 00:27:51,280
It seems like your brain
isn't as empty as I thought.

346
00:28:06,840 --> 00:28:08,440
‪-There they are.
‪-Over there.

347
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:09,880
Luke! Shang Zhitao.

348
00:28:09,960 --> 00:28:11,480
They are there. We found them.

349
00:28:11,560 --> 00:28:12,520
- Over there!
- It's them!

350
00:28:12,600 --> 00:28:14,280
- That's them.
- Looks like they're hurt.

351
00:28:14,360 --> 00:28:15,200
‪Call 120.

352
00:28:15,280 --> 00:28:16,120
‪Get them to a hospital.

353
00:28:39,200 --> 00:28:42,960
HEALTH FIRST, EXPERT CARE

354
00:29:43,160 --> 00:29:44,000
Nurse,

355
00:29:44,840 --> 00:29:46,280
where is the guy on the bed?

356
00:29:46,360 --> 00:29:47,840
Passed out
due to an intracranial hemorrhage.

357
00:29:47,920 --> 00:29:49,040
He was just sent to a major hospital
for emergency treatment.

358
00:29:51,880 --> 00:29:52,720
He…

359
00:29:53,360 --> 00:29:55,560
But he was fine last night.

360
00:29:55,640 --> 00:29:56,760
Most acute damage only appears

361
00:29:56,840 --> 00:29:58,840
several hours
after the wound is inflicted.

362
00:29:58,920 --> 00:30:01,200
You won't notice it at the time,
and when you do, it's too late.

363
00:30:02,400 --> 00:30:03,920
Where is he? I have to find him.

364
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:05,040
Wait.

365
00:30:05,920 --> 00:30:07,120
What's the hurry?

366
00:30:09,360 --> 00:30:11,840
Aren't you the one
being rushed to emergency?

367
00:30:13,200 --> 00:30:14,320
Can you not jinx me?

368
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:15,880
It's the other patient.

369
00:30:21,720 --> 00:30:22,920
The filming is over.

370
00:30:23,440 --> 00:30:24,680
I'll send you back to Beijing later.

371
00:30:25,280 --> 00:30:26,560
I hope I didn't cause any delays.

372
00:30:27,560 --> 00:30:30,280
Now is not the time for this.

373
00:30:42,280 --> 00:30:43,240
Eat now.

374
00:30:59,960 --> 00:31:02,440
Flora. Let's reflect on your work.

375
00:31:03,160 --> 00:31:06,160
Do you think you handled
this project well?

376
00:31:07,280 --> 00:31:09,240
I shouldn't have acted on my own.

377
00:31:09,760 --> 00:31:11,280
I lacked danger awareness.

378
00:31:12,360 --> 00:31:13,760
I caused trouble for everyone.

379
00:31:15,400 --> 00:31:16,600
What about teamwork?

380
00:31:18,080 --> 00:31:18,920
It was good.

381
00:31:21,760 --> 00:31:23,480
You still haven't realized
the problem, have you?

382
00:31:24,560 --> 00:31:25,880
Is Kitty your boss?

383
00:31:27,840 --> 00:31:29,560
Lumi and you are my bosses.

384
00:31:29,640 --> 00:31:31,520
Kitty is just a senior.

385
00:31:33,600 --> 00:31:34,640
A senior.

386
00:31:35,480 --> 00:31:37,120
There are many seniors in the office.

387
00:31:37,640 --> 00:31:41,160
Can a senior staff member
boss you around in your project?

388
00:31:41,760 --> 00:31:43,720
What's the point
of your project lead then?

389
00:31:47,760 --> 00:31:50,480
Are you going to ask me
to resign again this time?

390
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:03,000
Rest up. Take care of yourself.

391
00:32:03,680 --> 00:32:04,640
Make sure to go through
with the follow-up examination.

392
00:32:05,920 --> 00:32:08,040
If you feel unwell, go to Lumi

393
00:32:09,080 --> 00:32:10,000
or me.

394
00:32:14,040 --> 00:32:15,560
Thank you for the advice, Luke.

395
00:32:16,160 --> 00:32:17,800
I will follow your advice from now on.

396
00:32:44,920 --> 00:32:47,040
What kind of job is this?

397
00:32:47,120 --> 00:32:48,840
You are a cripple now.

398
00:32:49,400 --> 00:32:50,560
Come. Let me do it.

399
00:32:50,640 --> 00:32:52,080
Stop. Let me do it.

400
00:32:52,880 --> 00:32:54,360
Knowing your situation,

401
00:32:55,160 --> 00:32:57,280
you'll probably have to rest
at home for six months. Come.

402
00:32:58,400 --> 00:33:00,080
Make the company
support you for ten years.

403
00:33:00,840 --> 00:33:02,560
The doctor said

404
00:33:02,640 --> 00:33:04,680
- my bone wasn't affected.
- Careful.

405
00:33:04,760 --> 00:33:08,040
Besides, Luan Nian got injured
while rescuing me as well.

406
00:33:08,720 --> 00:33:10,960
Now is not the time to be selfless.

407
00:33:12,320 --> 00:33:13,600
They are two different things.

408
00:33:13,680 --> 00:33:15,280
You got injured during work,

409
00:33:15,360 --> 00:33:16,200
so the company
must take full responsibility.

410
00:33:23,160 --> 00:33:24,920
As for Luan Nian…

411
00:33:25,000 --> 00:33:26,400
For saving your life,

412
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:28,120
devote yourself to him.

413
00:33:28,640 --> 00:33:29,520
Then, you're even.

414
00:33:29,600 --> 00:33:31,800
- How sweet.
- Your job habit is coming out.

415
00:33:34,120 --> 00:33:35,080
No.

416
00:33:35,720 --> 00:33:37,880
He is a bad person.

417
00:33:37,960 --> 00:33:39,640
He gave you a hard time.

418
00:33:39,720 --> 00:33:40,720
He asked you to resign.

419
00:33:40,800 --> 00:33:41,760
That's workplace bullying.

420
00:33:41,840 --> 00:33:43,560
No. He's a bad person.

421
00:33:43,640 --> 00:33:45,360
How can our Tao fall for him?

422
00:33:45,440 --> 00:33:46,720
No. Not at all.

423
00:33:46,800 --> 00:33:47,960
You misunderstood.

424
00:33:48,040 --> 00:33:49,600
He is

425
00:33:50,200 --> 00:33:52,480
cold-faced and sharp-tongued,
but kind on the inside.

426
00:33:52,560 --> 00:33:55,520
Look. He cares
about his subordinates' safety.

427
00:33:56,560 --> 00:33:58,440
And he teaches me many things.

428
00:33:58,520 --> 00:34:00,960
I think I might have
misjudged him previously.

429
00:34:01,040 --> 00:34:02,440
- He…
- Shang Zhitao.

430
00:34:03,440 --> 00:34:05,160
Did you notice that?

431
00:34:07,640 --> 00:34:08,719
I…

432
00:34:08,800 --> 00:34:09,880
Notice what?

433
00:34:09,960 --> 00:34:12,960
You're defending him.

434
00:34:13,760 --> 00:34:15,320
You're praising him.

435
00:34:22,440 --> 00:34:24,880
I'm just being objective, okay?

436
00:34:26,120 --> 00:34:27,159
Objective, right.

437
00:34:27,760 --> 00:34:29,920
He came to my rescue alone.

438
00:34:30,440 --> 00:34:31,960
Anyone would be moved by that.

439
00:34:32,040 --> 00:34:33,679
Yes, he came to your rescue alone.

440
00:34:33,760 --> 00:34:35,120
You two saved each other.

441
00:34:35,199 --> 00:34:36,880
I am so moved by it.

442
00:34:38,080 --> 00:34:39,080
Shang Zhitao.

443
00:34:39,840 --> 00:34:41,480
Listen.

444
00:34:41,560 --> 00:34:43,920
Be brave when you have to.

445
00:34:44,000 --> 00:34:47,120
Don't miss out on the perfect guy
you ran into with your life.

446
00:34:54,120 --> 00:34:55,600
Why isn't Zhu back yet?

447
00:34:55,679 --> 00:34:57,920
Didn't he mention
he'd make pork rib soup today?

448
00:34:58,000 --> 00:35:00,520
Oh, my mom even bought
the Harbin red sausages

449
00:35:00,600 --> 00:35:02,240
that you like.

450
00:35:02,320 --> 00:35:03,320
- Changing the topic?
- We…

451
00:35:03,400 --> 00:35:04,760
Okay. I get it.

452
00:35:04,840 --> 00:35:06,200
Let me call Zhu now

453
00:35:06,280 --> 00:35:07,720
so that he'll come back
to boil the pork rib soup

454
00:35:07,800 --> 00:35:08,840
and give you the nutrients you need.

455
00:35:27,680 --> 00:35:28,920
Anything you want to add?

456
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:29,920
- That's all.
- Nothing.

457
00:35:30,000 --> 00:35:31,920
- That's all.
- Sign the contract then.

458
00:35:32,440 --> 00:35:34,080
- Okay.
- That's all.

459
00:35:34,160 --> 00:35:35,000
Dismissed.

460
00:35:36,720 --> 00:35:38,080
I'm heading to Finance.

461
00:36:06,400 --> 00:36:07,640
Colin, bring my laptop over.

462
00:36:07,720 --> 00:36:08,920
Luan Nian.

463
00:36:10,920 --> 00:36:13,880
I heard someone
almost died in your project.

464
00:36:14,400 --> 00:36:15,320
That is scary.

465
00:36:16,120 --> 00:36:18,240
I hope the client
didn't give you a hard time.

466
00:36:18,320 --> 00:36:20,160
Projects always come with risks.

467
00:36:20,920 --> 00:36:22,720
After all, not everyone can rely on luck

468
00:36:22,800 --> 00:36:25,960
and copy someone else's idea as you do.

469
00:36:26,040 --> 00:36:29,040
Ideas are meant to bounce off each other.

470
00:36:29,960 --> 00:36:31,320
The difference
between inspiration and plagiarism

471
00:36:31,400 --> 00:36:34,240
is similar to the difference
between a professional and you.

472
00:36:35,080 --> 00:36:36,280
How is it?

473
00:36:36,360 --> 00:36:38,480
Did you enjoy cleaning up the huge mess
you snatched from me?

474
00:36:39,160 --> 00:36:41,480
That's one of Lime's biggest clients.

475
00:36:42,800 --> 00:36:44,240
Of course, it is.

476
00:36:44,320 --> 00:36:46,000
But somehow, when you manage it,

477
00:36:46,520 --> 00:36:48,600
half of the client's budget is axed,

478
00:36:48,680 --> 00:36:50,480
and you had to work overtime
to fix the presentation deck.

479
00:36:51,240 --> 00:36:52,360
How's your sleep?

480
00:36:52,440 --> 00:36:53,920
Your eye bags
are about to fall on the floor.

481
00:36:57,800 --> 00:36:59,440
Don't you have work to do?

482
00:37:09,880 --> 00:37:10,720
Flora.

483
00:37:11,240 --> 00:37:12,240
Lumi.

484
00:37:12,320 --> 00:37:13,880
Why did you come to work?

485
00:37:13,960 --> 00:37:15,400
You can barely walk.

486
00:37:15,480 --> 00:37:16,560
It's fine. I went to get
my follow-up examination.

487
00:37:16,640 --> 00:37:18,200
The doctor said
I just needed to rest for two days.

488
00:37:18,280 --> 00:37:19,160
I forgot to take my laptop,

489
00:37:19,240 --> 00:37:21,040
so I came to check on everything.

490
00:37:21,720 --> 00:37:23,600
This is a work injury.

491
00:37:24,480 --> 00:37:26,280
Lime will not exploit you.

492
00:37:26,360 --> 00:37:27,920
They even bought insurance for you.

493
00:37:28,000 --> 00:37:30,040
Just stay at home and rest up.

494
00:37:30,760 --> 00:37:31,760
Go back.

495
00:37:33,240 --> 00:37:37,040
Actually, I want to thank Luke.

496
00:37:38,120 --> 00:37:39,360
Of course.

497
00:37:39,440 --> 00:37:41,200
But don't buy him any gifts.

498
00:37:41,280 --> 00:37:42,960
You can buy him a meal.

499
00:37:44,120 --> 00:37:44,960
I'll think about it.

500
00:37:45,040 --> 00:37:46,320
Yes!

501
00:37:46,400 --> 00:37:47,720
A new record.

502
00:37:47,800 --> 00:37:49,560
We got it. We are just too amazing.

503
00:37:50,640 --> 00:37:51,920
What a stellar result.

504
00:38:05,880 --> 00:38:07,800
I need to share something with you.

505
00:38:08,840 --> 00:38:09,760
I just got news

506
00:38:09,840 --> 00:38:13,640
that our team
secured the Mulanshuo project

507
00:38:13,720 --> 00:38:15,240
for annual advertising.

508
00:38:20,840 --> 00:38:23,880
Thank you for your hard work
the past three months.

509
00:38:24,400 --> 00:38:27,960
But as usual, we'll celebrate later.

510
00:38:28,560 --> 00:38:30,280
We still have work to finish.

511
00:38:30,360 --> 00:38:32,680
Make sure the online operations
go smoothly this week.

512
00:38:33,280 --> 00:38:37,280
We'll gather here every morning
at 8:00 a.m. for a daily briefing report.

513
00:38:37,360 --> 00:38:39,120
- Okay?
- Sure.

514
00:38:40,960 --> 00:38:42,120
‪Give it a quick touch-up.

515
00:38:46,280 --> 00:38:48,960
While everyone's here today,
let's have a recap of the project.

516
00:38:50,880 --> 00:38:52,800
As you all know,
a major incident took place

517
00:38:53,760 --> 00:38:54,800
during the day of filming.

518
00:38:57,720 --> 00:38:58,600
Mr. Luan,

519
00:38:58,680 --> 00:39:01,760
I meant to find
an opportunity to explain to you.

520
00:39:01,840 --> 00:39:03,240
I wasn't shirking my duty that day.

521
00:39:03,320 --> 00:39:04,920
The script was changed last minute,

522
00:39:05,000 --> 00:39:07,000
so I needed
to discuss it with the director.

523
00:39:07,080 --> 00:39:09,160
I was busy, so I asked Flora to help me.

524
00:39:09,960 --> 00:39:12,080
I'll make sure
to keep this in mind moving forward.

525
00:39:12,880 --> 00:39:14,760
So what's the point
of sending you over to assist?

526
00:39:15,360 --> 00:39:16,200
I…

527
00:39:16,880 --> 00:39:19,880
I didn't know Shang Zhitao was new here.

528
00:39:19,960 --> 00:39:21,640
I thought she could handle it.

529
00:39:21,720 --> 00:39:24,440
And everyone said
that she knew that place very well,

530
00:39:24,520 --> 00:39:25,760
so I let her handle it.

531
00:39:26,480 --> 00:39:27,600
Who is everyone?

532
00:39:32,600 --> 00:39:35,640
My management style is quite simple.
Regardless of your experience,

533
00:39:35,720 --> 00:39:37,840
those who won't take responsibility
will be replaced

534
00:39:37,920 --> 00:39:39,800
by those who will.

535
00:39:41,800 --> 00:39:43,600
Flora is new.

536
00:39:43,680 --> 00:39:45,400
She wanted to prove herself

537
00:39:45,480 --> 00:39:46,320
and was eager to take on tasks.

538
00:39:46,400 --> 00:39:47,560
- I can't stop her.
- Kitty.

539
00:39:48,800 --> 00:39:51,160
You have not been promoted
for three years.

540
00:39:51,240 --> 00:39:53,480
I understand that you see
the new hire as a threat,

541
00:39:54,480 --> 00:39:56,560
but that doesn't mean you should lie.

542
00:39:57,080 --> 00:40:01,040
Shang Zhitao invited the director
over from Guangzhou herself.

543
00:40:01,560 --> 00:40:04,720
What do you mean she needed you
to manage the director?

544
00:40:08,840 --> 00:40:10,120
What's done is done.

545
00:40:10,200 --> 00:40:11,960
Now, we need to solve the problem.

546
00:40:12,840 --> 00:40:13,960
This time, everyone
on the management level,

547
00:40:14,040 --> 00:40:15,280
including me, has to take accountability.

548
00:40:15,360 --> 00:40:17,240
One, it was our oversight.

549
00:40:17,320 --> 00:40:18,200
Two,

550
00:40:19,440 --> 00:40:21,160
we did not train
our new employee adequately.

551
00:40:22,320 --> 00:40:25,400
Lime will punish all relevant personnel,

552
00:40:25,480 --> 00:40:26,880
including me.

553
00:40:38,680 --> 00:40:42,000
Lumi's report yesterday
mentioned Flora specifically.

554
00:40:42,640 --> 00:40:44,520
I plan to confirm her position.

555
00:40:44,600 --> 00:40:45,960
Are you okay with it?

556
00:40:46,040 --> 00:40:48,480
<i>You have the final say.</i>
<i>I can never say no.</i>

557
00:40:49,880 --> 00:40:52,120
And I thought you finally
acknowledged her capabilities

558
00:40:52,200 --> 00:40:53,840
and my taste.

559
00:40:54,600 --> 00:40:57,200
<i>You sure have a peculiar taste.</i>

560
00:40:58,360 --> 00:41:00,800
So, I'll proceed then.

561
00:41:04,480 --> 00:41:05,520
Look at this.

562
00:41:09,080 --> 00:41:11,040
LIME ADVERTISING EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT

563
00:41:11,120 --> 00:41:12,960
EMPLOYEE: SHANG ZHITAO

564
00:41:13,560 --> 00:41:15,200
Employment contract?

565
00:41:15,760 --> 00:41:18,840
Your performance
in your first position was impressive.

566
00:41:18,920 --> 00:41:20,280
I have talked to Luke.

567
00:41:20,360 --> 00:41:22,880
He agreed to let you stay
at Business Division One.

568
00:41:22,960 --> 00:41:24,160
Do you want the position?

569
00:41:26,200 --> 00:41:27,320
Yes.

570
00:41:27,920 --> 00:41:28,920
Then, sign the contract.

571
00:41:30,240 --> 00:41:31,360
Thank you, Tracy.

572
00:41:31,440 --> 00:41:32,400
No need to thank me.

573
00:41:32,480 --> 00:41:35,680
Everyone saw how diligent
and responsible you are.

574
00:41:36,200 --> 00:41:38,200
You earned the contract yourself.

575
00:41:38,280 --> 00:41:39,360
Keep it up.

576
00:41:40,120 --> 00:41:42,280
I… I'll continue to work hard.

577
00:41:42,960 --> 00:41:46,440
Beijing is harsh but fair.

578
00:41:46,520 --> 00:41:48,120
But in Lime,

579
00:41:48,200 --> 00:41:50,440
if you work hard,
you will get something back.

580
00:42:06,400 --> 00:42:08,560
<i>Do you have time?</i>

581
00:42:08,640 --> 00:42:12,080
<i>I would like</i>
<i>to buy you a meal to thank you.</i>

582
00:42:15,680 --> 00:42:16,520
<i>No need.</i>

583
00:42:24,160 --> 00:42:26,360
<i>I'll buy you a meal tonight.</i>
<i>Send me the address.</i>

584
00:42:26,960 --> 00:42:27,960
<i>I'll pick you up.</i>

585
00:43:32,560 --> 00:43:33,600
Hug me tighter.

586
00:43:44,240 --> 00:43:45,160
Careful.
